      "writtenOn": "2023-09-07T17:22:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think you should set a default log level and we should only actually mark the disable logs for verbose entries.\n\n```\n// Log all D-Bus at verbose level. For especially verbose calls and callbacks, this needs to be explicitly disabled.\nconst DEFAULT_DBUS_LOGGING_CONFIG \u003d DbusLog::Enable(DbusLogOptions::LogAll, DbusLogVerbosity::Verbose);\n\nlet dbus_method_name \u003d meta_list.nested[0].clone();\nlet dbus_logging \u003d if meta_list.nested.len() \u003e 1 {\n  meta_list.nested[1].clone()\n} else {\n  DEFAULT_DBUS_LOGGING_CONFIG.clone()\n}\n```",
      "revId": "2161651b771ed62aabe5268f7f5b6d24e7fee6b0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f52ffdeb_611a0a2a",
        "filename": "system/gd/rust/linux/dbus_projection/dbus_macros/src/lib.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 128,
      "author": {
        "id": 1960535
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-08T11:15:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The problem with this is\n(1) we depend on dbus_projection to be able to reference to DbusLog, but dbus_projection itself depends on dbus_macros so it will make a circular dependency.\n(2) the data type of meta_list.nested[x] is NestedMeta, therefore is different from the data type of DEFAULT_DBUS_LOGGING_CONFIG.\n\nFor (1) we can define a third crate just to have these DbusLogXXX enums, so there are no circular dependency.\nFor (2) we can define it like this, or something\n```\nDEFAULT_DBUS_LOGGING_CONFIG \u003d syn::parse2::\u003cNestedMeta\u003e(quote! {\n  DbusLog::Enable(DbusLogOptions::LogAll, DbusLogVerbosity::Verbose)\n});\n```\nnow both are of NestedMeta type (and that avoids problem (1) as well since we don\u0027t really refer to DbusLog)",
      "parentUuid": "bc211977_a5ab685c",
      "revId": "2161651b771ed62aabe5268f7f5b6d24e7fee6b0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
