      "writtenOn": "2023-09-11T21:28:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not a fan of moving the parsing into the proc macro like this. Can we change logging Enabled and Disabled enum into separate structs and store it as a generic for logging?\n\n```\nstruct DBusLog\u003cT\u003e {\n  details: T\n}\n\ntrait DbusLogging {\n  fn format();\n}\n\nstruct LoggingDisabled;\nimpl DbusLogging for LoggingDisabled {\n  fn format(){}\n}\n\nstruct LoggingEnabled(DBusLogOptions, DBusLogVerbosity);\nimpl DBusLogging for LoggingEnabled {\n  fn format() -\u003e Option\u003cString\u003e {\n    let log_options \u003d \u0026self.0;\n    let log_verbosity \u003d \u0026self.1;\n    \n    // ... rest of logging implementation\n  }\n}\n```",
      "parentUuid": "a795b7e6_f8e78ec9",
      "revId": "2161651b771ed62aabe5268f7f5b6d24e7fee6b0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
