      "message": "Adding `impl fmt::Debug for Box\u003c...\u003e` works to some extent, but it complains when the DBus exporter is located in a different crate than the Boxed callback, e.g. `IBluetoothMediaCallback` is defined in `btstack` but the DBus exporter is in `btadapterd`.\n\nThe error is:\n```\n`IBluetoothMediaCallback` is not defined in the current crate\n`std::alloc::Global` is not defined in the current crate\nimpl doesn\u0027t use only types from inside the current crate\n```\n[1] suggests there is a \"trait coherence rule\" which is violated.\n\nTherefore I\u0027m adding a function in the DBusArg trait in ps#3 to format the string instead. PTAL.\n\n[1] https://blog.yossarian.net/2022/07/25/age-encryption-in-python-with-pyrage",
